## ECS Task Role (Least Privilege)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "ReadSecretsManager",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["secretsmanager:GetSecretValue"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:secretsmanager:ap-south-1:123456:secret:/prod/myapp/*"
    },
    {
      "Sid": "S3AppBucket",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::my-app-bucket/*"
    },
    {
      "Sid": "SQSQueue",
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["sqs:SendMessage", "sqs:ReceiveMessage", "sqs:DeleteMessage"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:sqs:ap-south-1:123456:my-app-queue"
    }
  ]
}
```

## Trust Policy

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": {"Service": "ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com"},
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole"
  }]
}
```

## Java SDK — DefaultCredentialsProvider Chain

```java
// SDK picks up credentials automatically:
// 1. Env vars → 2. System properties → 3. ~/.aws/credentials → 4. ECS task role
S3Client s3 = S3Client.builder()
    .credentialsProvider(DefaultCredentialsProvider.create())
    .region(Region.AP_SOUTH_1)
    .build();
// On ECS: automatically uses task role, no keys in code
```

## Cross-Account Pattern

```
Account A (Prod): 111111
  ECS Task → STS.AssumeRole → Account B role

Account B (Shared Services): 222222
  Role: shared-s3-reader
    Trust: 111111:role/prod-ecs-task-role can assume this
    Policy: s3:GetObject on shared-artifacts/*
```

## Trust Policy in Account B

```json
{
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": {
      "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::111111:role/prod-ecs-task-role"
    },
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
    "Condition": {
      "StringEquals": {"sts:ExternalId": "my-external-id-123"}
    }
  }]
}
```

## Java SDK Cross-Account Client

```java
@Bean
public S3Client sharedServicesS3Client() {
    AwsCredentialsProvider crossAccountCreds =
        StsAssumeRoleCredentialsProvider.builder()
            .stsClient(StsClient.create())
            .refreshRequest(AssumeRoleRequest.builder()
                .roleArn("arn:aws:iam::222222:role/shared-s3-reader")
                .roleSessionName("prod-app-cross-account")
                .externalId("my-external-id-123")
                .durationSeconds(3600)
                .build())
            .build();

    return S3Client.builder()
        .credentialsProvider(crossAccountCreds)
        .region(Region.AP_SOUTH_1)
        .build();
}
```

## Spring Security Configuration

```yaml
spring:
  security:
    oauth2:
      resourceserver:
        jwt:
          jwk-set-uri: https://cognito-idp.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/ap-south-1_XXXXXXXXX/.well-known/jwks.json
          issuer-uri: https://cognito-idp.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com/ap-south-1_XXXXXXXXX
```

```java
@Configuration
@EnableWebSecurity
@EnableMethodSecurity
public class SecurityConfig {

    @Bean
    public SecurityFilterChain filterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
        return http
            .csrf(csrf -> csrf.disable())
            .sessionManagement(s -> s.sessionCreationPolicy(STATELESS))
            .authorizeHttpRequests(auth -> auth
                .requestMatchers("/actuator/health").permitAll()
                .requestMatchers("/api/admin/**").hasRole("ADMIN")
                .anyRequest().authenticated()
            )
            .oauth2ResourceServer(oauth2 -> oauth2
                .jwt(jwt -> jwt.jwtAuthenticationConverter(cognitoJwtConverter()))
            )
            .build();
    }

    @Bean
    public JwtAuthenticationConverter cognitoJwtConverter() {
        JwtAuthenticationConverter converter = new JwtAuthenticationConverter();
        converter.setJwtGrantedAuthoritiesConverter(jwt -> {
            List<String> groups = jwt.getClaimAsStringList("cognito:groups");
            if (groups == null) return List.of();
            return groups.stream()
                .map(g -> new SimpleGrantedAuthority("ROLE_" + g.toUpperCase()))
                .toList();
        });
        return converter;
    }
}

// Controller: access Cognito user info from JWT
@GetMapping("/api/profile")
public UserProfile getProfile(@AuthenticationPrincipal Jwt jwt) {
    String userId = jwt.getSubject();
    String email  = jwt.getClaimAsString("email");
    return userService.getOrCreate(userId, email);
}
```

## Permission Boundaries

```json
// Developer's role: broad identity policy
// Policy attached to developer role:
{
  "Statement": [{"Effect": "Allow", "Action": "s3:*", "Resource": "*"}]
}

// Permission boundary attached to same role:
{
  "Statement": [{"Effect": "Allow", "Action": "s3:GetObject", "Resource": "*"}]
}

// Effective: only s3:GetObject  (intersection)
// s3:PutObject: identity allows it, boundary doesn't → DENIED
```

## SCP: Restrict Account to One Region

```json
// SCP applied to dev-account OU:
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "DenyOutsideApSouth1",
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "NotAction": [
        "iam:*",
        "sts:*",
        "support:*",
        "cloudfront:*"
      ],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringNotEquals": {
          "aws:RequestedRegion": "ap-south-1"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "Sid": "DenyRootAccountUsage",
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "*",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringLike": {
          "aws:PrincipalArn": "arn:aws:iam::*:root"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Permission Evaluation Logic

```
Request arrives →
1. Is there an explicit DENY anywhere? → DENIED immediately
2. Is there an SCP that allows this? → if no → DENIED
3. Does the permission boundary allow this? → if no → DENIED
4. Does the identity policy allow this? → if no → DENIED (implicit deny)
5. All checks pass → ALLOWED
```
